  "question": {
    "text": "In the circuit shown here, the voltage across $\\mathrm{E}$ and $\\mathrm{C}$ are respectively $300 \\mathrm{~V}$ and $400 \\mathrm{~V}$. The voltage $\\mathrm{E}$ of the ac source is :\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/YSP4MM9BEDO78fWILiVDleUky9_Ezn_8B4xtE3kK1gA.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "H2PTr",
      "text": "\n$400$ Volt\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "k834v",
      "text": "\n$500$ Volt\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hiRXc",
      "text": "\n$100$ Volt\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "A9Rks",
      "text": "\n$700$ Volt",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Voltage $E$ of the ac source\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& E=V_C-V_L \\\\\n& =400 \\mathrm{~V}-300 \\mathrm{~V}=100 \\mathrm{~V}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
